camchrome: Windows persona text metrics and anti-aliasing in every process; local() by full name.

1014/1015 did not reach the audit's numbers:
- Font-size stepping still changed the width on ~60% of 0.01 px steps: FreeType sets the size in
  26.6 fixed point (1/64 px), so linear advances move in steps whatever the hinting. Under a
  Windows persona Skia's FreeType scaler now takes advances from design units scaled by the
  exact float size, as DirectWrite computes them (CAMCHROME_FT_FLOAT_ADVANCES).
- The anti-aliasing ladder was set in the renderer only, while an accelerated canvas's glyphs
  are rasterised in the GPU process, which gets no fingerprint switches. The browser now sets
  CAMCHROME_FT_COVERAGE_LEVELS=16 before any child starts, and Skia reads it in every process.
- local() looked the clone up by its family name; unique names are the full and PostScript
  names ("Carlito Regular", "Carlito-Regular"), which are tried now.

--- a/third_party/skia/src/ports/SkFontHost_FreeType.cpp
+++ b/third_party/skia/src/ports/SkFontHost_FreeType.cpp
@@ -47,12 +47,31 @@
 #include <array>
